## 4. How a <module> is built (if L3·microservices)
```
services/<name>/            # single template for every module
├── src/index.ts            # entry: buildApp() + bus + shutdown
├── src/...routes/          # typed routes, mirror the OpenAPI contract
├── src/...events/          # publish + subscribe (sagas, idempotency)
├── src/db/ + migrations/   # schema + SQL migrations
└── test/                   # health / contract / integration
```

## 5. Working rules (top 5–8)
- **Contract-first:** every endpoint exists in `contracts/openapi/<svc>.yaml` before any code.
- **Contracts are machine truth:** change behavior → change the contract first.
- **Events:** format `pmos.<svc>.<resource>.<action>` (`created|updated|deleted`); payload camelCase; version required.
- **Close a feature end-to-end** (📋→✅): full checklist in `AGENT.md` (contract → catalog → schema → migrate → routes → events → tests → doc counters → commit gate).
- **Module isolation:** no reading another module's storage.
- **Typing:** no `any`/`@ts-ignore`; timestamps ISO.

## 6. Definition of Done (from `AGENT.md` §gate)
Green: typecheck _N/N_, build _N/N_, contract _N/N_, tests _P/Q_, cross-module sagas §1–N, compose up no flips, hygiene. Commit gate — `AGENT.md`.

